        <h2>1. General Risk Warning</h2>
        <p>Trading in financial markets, including but not limited to forex, cryptocurrencies, commodities, indices, and stocks, carries substantial risk. The value of investments can go up as well as down, and you may not get back the amount you originally invested. Past performance is not a reliable indicator of future results.</p>

        <h2>2. Leverage Risk</h2>
        <p>Leveraged trading can magnify both gains and losses. A small market movement against your position may result in a total loss of your margin. You should fully understand how leverage works and only use it if you are comfortable with the increased risk.</p>

        <h2>3. Volatility Risk</h2>
        <p>Cryptocurrency and commodity markets are particularly volatile. Prices can change rapidly and unpredictably, which may lead to significant losses in a short period.</p>

        <h2>4. No Guarantee of Returns</h2>
        <p>VelocityX does not guarantee any specific return on investment. Any projections, signals, or analysis provided on the platform are for informational purposes only and do not constitute financial advice. You are solely responsible for your trading decisions.</p>

        <h2>5. Technology Risk</h2>
        <p>The Service relies on internet connectivity, servers, and software. Technical failures, outages, or cyber attacks may prevent you from accessing your account or executing trades at critical moments, potentially resulting in financial loss.</p>

        <h2>6. Regulatory Risk</h2>
        <p>Regulations governing financial trading vary by jurisdiction and may change. You are responsible for ensuring that your use of the Service complies with all applicable laws in your country of residence.</p>

        <h2>7. Third-Party Risk</h2>
        <p>VelocityX may integrate third-party tools, data feeds, and payment processors. We are not responsible for losses caused by the failure or inaccuracy of third-party services.</p>

        <h2>8. Your Responsibility</h2>
        <p>Before trading, you should:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Assess your financial situation and risk tolerance honestly</li>
          <li>Only trade with funds you can afford to lose entirely</li>
          <li>Educate yourself about the markets and instruments you trade</li>
          <li>Consider seeking independent financial advice from a licensed professional</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>9. Acceptance</h2>
        <p>By using the VelocityX platform, you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and accepted the risks described in this disclaimer. You agree that VelocityX is not liable for any losses you incur as a result of your trading activity.</p>

